{"kind":"event","event_id":7026,"event_uid":"01M2NNPSYE19DG66JDD765JZRZ","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":300,"issue_uid":"01M2NNMB9JMCQD9BEM7HPF0GF7","issue_short_id":"0gf7","actor":"impl:A@run-164","hlc_physical_ms":1789581289422,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"531524e28fd034f5c5d345c8b0568fc68d363a8c9643bbd9f83ec96b85fbae74","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NNPSYDW3J3NTD21FM7915T","author":"impl:A@run-164","body":"Task A approach: add derive_regenerate_cmd(root) beside derive_bootstrap_cmd in skills/ultrapowers/scripts/ultra_run.py — same file-presence ladder, same precedence (pnpm > bun > npm under package.json; uv.lock then pyproject [tool.uv without), but the unfrozen/lockfile-writing form of each command, and (None, 'package-json') for a bare package.json since there is no lockfile to rebuild. requirements.txt derives nothing (there is no lockfile). Then mirror the stamping at the preflight's --bootstrap-cmd 'else' branch only: args_obj['regenerateCmd'] guarded on truth, receipt['regenerateCmd']/['regenerateCmdSource'] ('detected:<rule>') likewise — so a knob-supplied or ''-disabled bootstrap derives no regenerator. No new stage, no --regenerate-cmd knob.","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:54:49.421406228Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:54:49.422Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7027,"event_uid":"01M2NNRWGM6X3D90PMYFMTJ4QQ","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":300,"issue_uid":"01M2NNMB9JMCQD9BEM7HPF0GF7","issue_short_id":"0gf7","actor":"exam:A@run-164","hlc_physical_ms":1789581357588,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"f749f2909e06b2f92862edb244945e908f9b881545f2e795ac8a36f3540138bd","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NNRWGJ1HHW29Y3BFK3R72K","author":"exam:A@run-164","body":"exam for A: appending the regenerator legs to the end of tests/test_ultra_run_bootstrap_cmd.py, under a comment naming the task, with `derive_regenerate_cmd` imported beside `derive_bootstrap_cmd` at line 30 exactly as the task's Context directs.\n\nLeg map:\n- (a) [M1] six rows, one test per rung-tree, full tuple equality: pnpm-lock.yaml, bun.lock, bun.lockb, package-lock.json (each beside package.json), then uv.lock and pyproject.toml [tool.uv] with no package.json.\n- (b) [M1] the three None rows: bare package.json -> (None,'package-json'); empty tree -> (None,None); requirements.txt only -> (None,None).\n- (c) [M1] precedence on one tree carrying pnpm+bun+npm lockfiles -> pnpm rung, then unlink pnpm -> bun rung; each row also asserts the rule equals derive_bootstrap_cmd's rule on the same tree ('the same order').\n- (d) [M2] real driver subprocess over a tmp_path git repo (package.json + bun.lock), reading .claude/ultrapowers/run-t1/args.json and run-t1/receipt.json off disk -- the leg names receipt.json, so the file, not just stdout.\n- (e) [M2] same preflight over a requirements.txt-only repo, and over the bun.lock repo under --bootstrap-cmd '', asserting both keys absent from both files. Plus the bare-package.json preflight row, which is M2's 'exactly when a command was derived' discriminator: bootstrapCmd is truthy there while regenerateCmd must be absent, so the guard cannot piggyback on `if bootstrap_cmd:`.\n\nReading I am recording so a later session need not reconstruct it: the module-level import of derive_regenerate_cmd makes the WHOLE file a collection error at BASE, not just the new legs. That is deliberate and is what the Context asks for -- the ImportError names the produced symbol, so the red reads as the absent implementation. The 19 pre-existing legs pass at BASE today (verified before touching the file).","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:55:57.586707682Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:55:57.588Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7028,"event_uid":"01M2NNSXWY434609HSZZ0DRN5T","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":300,"issue_uid":"01M2NNMB9JMCQD9BEM7HPF0GF7","issue_short_id":"0gf7","actor":"impl:A@run-164","hlc_physical_ms":1789581391774,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"deace8e207618bcb4b5f047b061f42d1e20481a36783b644a9e03c82629d57c3","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NNSXWWAB95VTG5Z06XY956","author":"impl:A@run-164","body":"Done and green. derive_regenerate_cmd lands at skills/ultrapowers/scripts/ultra_run.py right after derive_bootstrap_cmd, same rungs/precedence in unfrozen form; (None,'package-json') for a bare package.json and (None,None) for a requirements.txt-only tree. Preflight stamps regenerateCmd into the args file and regenerateCmd/regenerateCmdSource ('detected:<rule>') into receipt.json, both guarded on truth and both only on the --bootstrap-cmd 'else' branch, so a knob-supplied or ''-disabled bootstrap derives no regenerator. Decision a later session would otherwise rediscover: no new preflight stage was added — the bootstrap-command stage's detail is unchanged, since existing legs pin that string exactly; the receipt's two keys are the only place the derivation is reported. Also appended one LLM_DERIVES entry saying the LLM derives nothing for regenerateCmd and that there is no knob for it (no test pins that list). Proofs: pytest tests/test_ultra_run_bootstrap_cmd.py 31 passed; fleet/roles/ untouched; test_sims_are_hermetic.mjs ALL TESTS PASSED. Neighbouring suites test_ultra_run{,_exam_command,_task_test_cmds}.py 81 passed.","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:56:31.772481758Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:56:31.774Z"}
